; Vendored, not scanned as first-party: dune builds these without applying this
; project's warning settings, and their own tests are not ours to run.
;
; [ocaml-model-explorer] carries its own [model-explorer] gitlink, which stays
; uninitialised on purpose -- it is the upstream TypeScript renderer, fetched
; from npm at the pinned version rather than built from source here.
;
; [err_trace] (module [Err]) is not vendored: it is the opam package, and
; melange builds use its [err_trace-melange] library.
;
; [bytesrw] is NOT built by dune at all -- it carries no dune files (upstream
; ships a topkg/ocamlbuild build), and this project consumes the real opam
; package. This checkout tracks github.com/dbuenzli/bytesrw for reference only,
; kept out of @fmt/@all the same way the others above are, since none of its
; ~60 files are ours to reformat or build.

; [ocaml-safetensors] and [ocaml-hf-hub] are standalone repos with their own
; test suites, fixtures and JavaScript build scripts; only the libraries that
; [lib/pt2_safetensors] depends on are built here. [ocaml-hf-hub] is the sans-IO
; Hub downloader; [ocaml-safetensors] supplies the bigstring/mmap reader.
; Its javascript/shared driver is not built here: js/pt2_safetensors_js copies it.

(vendored_dirs
 ocaml-hf-hub
 ocaml-model-explorer
 ocaml-safetensors
 ocaml-yamlt
 opickle
 bytesrw)

; [rivet] and [rivet-compcert] are not built in this workspace: the image
; installs both as opam packages from these checkouts (make
; compcert.embed.install), because rivet_compcert's embedding needs an
; out-of-tree CompCert build. Dune must not see their projects.

(data_only_dirs rivet rivet-compcert)
